</span><span><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INNER</span></span><span> </span>=
<span><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">JOIN</span></span><span> table2 </span><=
span><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ON</span></span><span> table1.colonne </s=
pan><span><span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span></span><span> table2.colo=
nne;
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<ul data-start=3D"1316" data-end=3D"1701">
<li data-start=3D"1316" data-end=3D"1413" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1318" data-end=3D"1413" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
318" data-end=3D"1339"><code data-start=3D"1320" data-end=3D"1337">SELECT c=
olonnes</code></strong> : S=C3=A9lectionnez les colonnes que vous souhaitez=
 afficher dans le r=C3=A9sultat.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1414" data-end=3D"1471" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1416" data-end=3D"1471" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
416" data-end=3D"1433"><code data-start=3D"1418" data-end=3D"1431">FROM tab=
le1</code></strong> : La premi=C3=A8re table dans la jointure.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1472" data-end=3D"1559" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1474" data-end=3D"1559" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
474" data-end=3D"1497"><code data-start=3D"1476" data-end=3D"1495">INNER JO=
IN table2</code></strong> : La deuxi=C3=A8me table avec laquelle vous effec=
tuez la jointure.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1560" data-end=3D"1701" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1562" data-end=3D"1701" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
562" data-end=3D"1602"><code data-start=3D"1564" data-end=3D"1600">ON table=
1.colonne =3D table2.colonne</code></strong> : La condition de jointure, c'=
est-=C3=A0-dire, sur quelle colonne les deux tables doivent =C3=AAtre reli=
=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"1703" data-end=3D"1754" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1707" data-end=3D"1754">3. Exemple de Jointure Interne (INNER JOIN)</strong=
></h3>
<h4 data-start=3D"1756" data-end=3D"1779" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1761" data-end=3D"1779">Exemple simple</strong></h4>
<p data-start=3D"1781" data-end=3D"1900" class=3D"">Imaginons deux tables d=
ans une base de donn=C3=A9es qui stocke des informations sur des <strong da=
ta-start=3D"1864" data-end=3D"1875">clients</strong> et leurs <strong data-=
start=3D"1885" data-end=3D"1898">commandes</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1902" data-end=3D"2204">
<li data-start=3D"1902" data-end=3D"2028" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1904" data-end=3D"1980" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
904" data-end=3D"1923">Table <code data-start=3D"1912" data-end=3D"1921">cl=
ients</code></strong> : Cette table contient les informations sur les clien=
ts.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1983" data-end=3D"2028">
<li data-start=3D"1983" data-end=3D"2025" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1985" data-end=3D"2025" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"198=
5" data-end=3D"1996">id_client</code> (cl=C3=A9 primaire), <code data-start=
=3D"2013" data-end=3D"2025">nom_client</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2029" data-end=3D"2204" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2031" data-end=3D"2114" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
031" data-end=3D"2052">Table <code data-start=3D"2039" data-end=3D"2050">co=
mmandes</code></strong> : Cette table contient les commandes pass=C3=A9es p=
ar les clients.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2117" data-end=3D"2204">
<li data-start=3D"2117" data-end=3D"2204" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2119" data-end=3D"2204" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"211=
9" data-end=3D"2132">id_commande</code> (cl=C3=A9 primaire), <code data-sta=
rt=3D"2149" data-end=3D"2160">id_client</code> (cl=C3=A9 =C3=A9trang=C3=A8r=
e), <code data-start=3D"2178" data-end=3D"2187">produit</code>, <code data-=
start=3D"2189" data-end=3D"2204">date_commande</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2206" data-end=3D"2352" class=3D"">Si vous souhaitez liste=
r tous les clients avec leurs commandes respectives, vous pouvez utiliser u=
ne jointure interne sur la colonne <code data-start=3D"2339" data-end=3D"23=
50">id_client</code> :</p>
<pre class=3D"!overflow-visible" data-start=3D"2354" data-end=3D"2487"><div=
