<p data-start=3D"2489" data-end=3D"2506" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
489" data-end=3D"2504">Explication</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2507" data-end=3D"2740">
<li data-start=3D"2507" data-end=3D"2614" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2509" data-end=3D"2614" class=3D"">Ce SQL va r=C3=A9cup=C3=
=A9rer les noms des clients (<code data-start=3D"2551" data-end=3D"2563">no=
m_client</code>) et les produits qu'ils ont command=C3=A9s (<code data-star=
t=3D"2603" data-end=3D"2612">produit</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2615" data-end=3D"2740" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2617" data-end=3D"2740" class=3D"">Il ne retournera que le=
s clients qui ont effectu=C3=A9 des commandes, car la jointure interne filt=
re les clients sans commandes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"2742" data-end=3D"2769" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2747" data-end=3D"2767">R=C3=A9sultat attendu</strong> :</h4>
<div class=3D"overflow-x-auto contain-inline-size"><table data-start=3D"277=
1" data-end=3D"2936" node=3D"[object Object]"><thead data-start=3D"2771" da=
ta-end=3D"2803"><tr data-start=3D"2771" data-end=3D"2803"><th data-start=3D=
"2771" data-end=3D"2785">nom_client</th><th data-start=3D"2785" data-end=3D=
"2803">produit</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start=3D"2837" data-end=3D"2936=
