<h3 data-start=3D"7764" data-end=3D"7785" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7768" data-end=3D"7785">6. Conclusion</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"7787" data-end=3D"8137" class=3D"">Les <strong data-start=
=3D"7791" data-end=3D"7813">jointures avanc=C3=A9es</strong> en SQL offrent=
 une flexibilit=C3=A9 accrue pour manipuler et analyser des donn=C3=A9es r=
=C3=A9parties entre plusieurs tables. En ma=C3=AEtrisant les <strong data-s=
tart=3D"7943" data-end=3D"7962">FULL OUTER JOIN</strong>, <strong data-star=
t=3D"7964" data-end=3D"7977">SELF JOIN</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"7979=
" data-end=3D"7995">NATURAL JOIN</strong>, ainsi que les concepts comme <st=
rong data-start=3D"8026" data-end=3D"8035">UNION</strong> et <strong data-s=
