<h2 data-start=3D"64" data-end=3D"125" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"67"=
 data-end=3D"123">1. Introduction =C3=A0 la Sauvegarde et =C3=A0 la Restaur=
ation</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"127" data-end=3D"565" class=3D"">La sauvegarde et la resta=
uration d=E2=80=99une base de donn=C3=A9es sont des t=C3=A2ches <strong dat=
a-start=3D"198" data-end=3D"211">critiques</strong> pour assurer la s=C3=A9=
curit=C3=A9 et la continuit=C3=A9 des donn=C3=A9es. Elles permettent de :<b=
r data-start=3D"288" data-end=3D"291">
=E2=9C=94 <strong data-start=3D"293" data-end=3D"332">Prot=C3=A9ger contre =
la perte de donn=C3=A9es</strong> due =C3=A0 des pannes mat=C3=A9rielles, d=
es erreurs humaines ou des cyberattaques.<br data-start=3D"405" data-end=3D=
"408">
=E2=9C=94 <strong data-start=3D"410" data-end=3D"441">Migrer des bases de d=
onn=C3=A9es</strong> vers un autre serveur ou une autre version du SGBD.<br=
 data-start=3D"493" data-end=3D"496">
=E2=9C=94 <strong data-start=3D"498" data-end=3D"526">Tester des modificati=
ons</strong> sans impacter la base de production.</p>
<p data-start=3D"567" data-end=3D"596" class=3D"">=F0=9F=92=A1 <strong data=
-start=3D"570" data-end=3D"592">Deux concepts cl=C3=A9s</strong> :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"597" data-end=3D"787">
<li data-start=3D"597" data-end=3D"689" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"599" data-end=3D"689" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"599=
" data-end=3D"622">Sauvegarde (Backup)</strong> : Cr=C3=A9ation d=E2=80=99u=
ne copie des donn=C3=A9es pour une r=C3=A9cup=C3=A9ration future.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"690" data-end=3D"787" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"692" data-end=3D"787" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"692=
" data-end=3D"718">Restauration (Restore)</strong> : Processus de r=C3=A9cu=
p=C3=A9ration des donn=C3=A9es =C3=A0 partir d=E2=80=99une sauvegarde.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"789" data-end=3D"792" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"794" data-end=3D"833" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"79=
7" data-end=3D"831">2. Types de Sauvegardes en SQL</strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"835" data-end=3D"931" class=3D"">Il existe plusieurs types=
 de sauvegardes, chacun ayant ses propres avantages et inconv=C3=A9nients.<=
/p>
<h3 data-start=3D"933" data-end=3D"981" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"93=
7" data-end=3D"979">2.1. Sauvegarde Compl=C3=A8te (Full Backup)</strong></h=
3>
<p data-start=3D"982" data-end=3D"1039" class=3D"">=F0=9F=93=8C <strong dat=
a-start=3D"985" data-end=3D"1037">Une copie int=C3=A9grale de toute la base=
 de donn=C3=A9es.</strong></p>
<p data-start=3D"1041" data-end=3D"1161" class=3D"">=E2=9C=94 Id=C3=A9al po=
ur une r=C3=A9cup=C3=A9ration compl=C3=A8te.<br data-start=3D"1080" data-en=
d=3D"1083">
=E2=9C=94 Facile =C3=A0 restaurer.<br data-start=3D"1104" data-end=3D"1107"=
>
=E2=9D=8C Peut =C3=AAtre volumineux et lent sur de grandes bases.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1163" data-end=3D"1201" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1167" data-end=3D"1199">2.2. Sauvegarde Incr=C3=A9mentale</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1202" data-end=3D"1308" class=3D"">=F0=9F=93=8C <strong da=
ta-start=3D"1205" data-end=3D"1306">Ne sauvegarde que les donn=C3=A9es modi=
fi=C3=A9es depuis la derni=C3=A8re sauvegarde (compl=C3=A8te ou incr=C3=A9m=
entale).</strong></p>
<p data-start=3D"1310" data-end=3D"1484" class=3D"">=E2=9C=94 Gagne du temp=
s et r=C3=A9duit l=E2=80=99espace disque.<br data-start=3D"1353" data-end=
=3D"1356">
=E2=9D=8C La restauration est plus complexe car elle n=C3=A9cessite la dern=
i=C3=A8re sauvegarde compl=C3=A8te + toutes les sauvegardes incr=C3=A9menta=
les.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1486" data-end=3D"1526" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1490" data-end=3D"1524">2.3. Sauvegarde Diff=C3=A9rentielle</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1527" data-end=3D"1615" class=3D"">=F0=9F=93=8C <strong da=
ta-start=3D"1530" data-end=3D"1613">Sauvegarde toutes les donn=C3=A9es modi=
fi=C3=A9es depuis la derni=C3=A8re sauvegarde compl=C3=A8te.</strong></p>
<p data-start=3D"1617" data-end=3D"1736" class=3D"">=E2=9C=94 Plus rapide q=
u=E2=80=99une sauvegarde compl=C3=A8te.<br data-start=3D"1658" data-end=3D"=
1661">
=E2=9D=8C Peut devenir volumineux si de nombreuses modifications sont effec=
tu=C3=A9es.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1738" data-end=3D"1805" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
1742" data-end=3D"1803">2.4. Sauvegarde des Journaux de Transactions (Log B=
ackup)</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"1806" data-end=3D"1886" class=3D"">=F0=9F=93=8C <strong da=
ta-start=3D"1809" data-end=3D"1884">Sauvegarde l=E2=80=99historique des tra=
nsactions depuis la derni=C3=A8re sauvegarde.</strong></p>
<p data-start=3D"1888" data-end=3D"2045" class=3D"">=E2=9C=94 Permet une r=
=C3=A9cup=C3=A9ration <strong data-start=3D"1914" data-end=3D"1931">point-i=
n-time</strong> (au moment exact avant un incident).<br data-start=3D"1968"=
 data-end=3D"1971">
=E2=9D=8C N=C3=A9cessite une bonne gestion pour =C3=A9viter un stockage exc=
essif des logs.</p>
